{"authored" [{"question" "q-130955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The row echelon form matrix $A$ is given below. What are its **non**-pivot columns?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b881bb3817b14744b5b3494377b9605a47e52a1496f2839e9be73e8e2dfdb05" "basis" 1449 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Remember that the pivots of a matrix in row echelon form are the first non-zero entries in each row of the matrix.\n\nWe can see that $A$ has $3$ pivots in the $1$st, $2$nd and $4$th columns:\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 9 & -5 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 6 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only non-pivot column is the $3$rd column." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b881bb3817b14744b5b3494377b9605a47e52a1496f2839e9be73e8e2dfdb05" "basis" 1449 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2c680fda06fa2f83e46075e6ebe9b567cd34ab2f0257707276276bc6230ca565" "basis" 1449 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/edb-import/verifica