port/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Determine the number of pivot columns of the matrix $B,$ given by\n\n$$\nB=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b881bb3817b14744b5b3494377b9605a47e52a1496f2839e9be73e8e2dfdb05" "basis" 1449 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we need to convert $B$ to row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 0 & 2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLooking at the row echelon form, we see that $A$ has $3$ pivots, and therefore the number of pivot columns is $3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/state.json" "file_sha256" "2b881bb3817b14744b5b3494377b9605a47e52a1496f2839e9be73e8e2dfdb05" "basis" 1449 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-130957" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040466/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "2